From 3b3662c2125d8e5de03398f5d9dc6a69158e329b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allen Kang <allen.kang@mitaccomputing.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 10:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix OperatingSystemState for OS boot progress

BootProgress can be updated by the BIOS through IPMI, independently of
the POST_COMPLETE GPIO.  OSStart and OSRunning were not handled when
translating BootProgress to OperatingSystemState.  Consequently, a
preceding PCIInit event left OperatingSystemState at Inactive even after
BootProgress reached OSRunning.

Keep the OS in Standby while it starts, and move it to BootComplete once
OSRunning is reported.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [No upstream maintenance]
---
 src/power_control.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/power_control.cpp b/src/power_control.cpp
index 1be9e89..30733b4 100644
--- a/src/power_control.cpp
+++ b/src/power_control.cpp
@@ -331,6 +331,12 @@ static int handleBootProgressStageChange(const BootProgressStages progress)
             case BootProgressStages::SystemSetup:
                 setOperatingSystemState(OperatingSystemOSStatus::Standby);
                 break;
+            case BootProgressStages::OSStart:
+                setOperatingSystemState(OperatingSystemOSStatus::Standby);
+                break;
+            case BootProgressStages::OSRunning:
+                setOperatingSystemState(OperatingSystemOSStatus::BootComplete);
+                break;
             default:
                 lg2::info(
                     "Host{HOST}: \"{PROGRESS}\" doesn't impact OperatingSystemOSStatus.",
-- 
